WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:34.458
In verse 14.13, Lord Krishna clarifies

2
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:36.208
how Tamo Guna, when it increases,

3
00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:40.166
affects a person’s conduct.

4
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:42.625
He has already described the effects of

5
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.000
sattva and rajas in the previous verses.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.750
When Tamo Guna becomes

7
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.083
dominant, confusion increases in life,

8
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.541
the power of effort weakens,

9
00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:56.500
and a person is drawn toward false thinking.

10
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.375
When Tamo Guna increases,

11
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:08.000
it blinds a person’s vision to reality.

12
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Clarity disappears –

13
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.875
this is called aprakasha.

14
00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:15.208
The tendency to act

15
00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.833
also disappears –

16
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.416
this is called apravritti.

17
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:22.791
In this state, pramada arises –

18
00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:24.083
where a person

19
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.250
becomes careless

20
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.833
about their duties and responsibilities.

21
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:31.541
Then moha takes over.

22
00:01:31.541 --> 00:01:34.458
A person begins to accept falsehood as truth.

23
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:36.916
Their understanding becomes confused.

24
00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:40.208
Sometimes they accept ideas

25
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:42.500
that have no basis,

26
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.958
or begin doing things that are harmful

27
00:01:45.958 --> 00:01:49.000
to themselves or others.

28
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.833
Such people lose viveka – discernment.

29
00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:53.541
They begin to act

30
00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:55.833
against their own interests.

31
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:58.916
They fall into destructive habits.

32
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:02.000
Some become victims of
intoxication or addiction.

33
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.666
And many get stuck

34
00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:06.083
in life situations

35
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:08.833
that stop their growth.

36
00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:11.833
When there is no light or direction, the soul

37
00:02:11.833 --> 00:02:16.625
sinks deeper into confusion and inertia.

38
00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:18.666
Lord Krishna warns

39
00:02:18.666 --> 00:02:21.541
that when Tamo Guna becomes dominant,

40
00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.416
these qualities bind a person

41
00:02:23.416 --> 00:02:28.916
and keep the soul trapped even longer
in the bondage of ignorance.

42
00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:35.458
Sometimes the mind

43
00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:37.291
begins to weave elaborate stories

44
00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:41.041
from the smallest of things.

45
00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:44.041
One word said by someone,

46
00:02:44.041 --> 00:02:47.333
or a brief delay in the day –

47
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:51.500
these start to feed the restlessness within.

48
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.416
But remember –

49
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:57.000
not every thought that arises in the mind

50
00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.125
deserves your attention.

51
00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:03.125
When Tamo Guna takes over,

52
00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:06.541
it does not only bring laziness.

53
00:03:06.541 --> 00:03:11.750
It fills you with darkness – aprakasha.

54
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.875
In this state

55
00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:15.958
you start believing things

56
00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:19.583
that are not even true.

57
00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:21.791
Life is not difficult,

58
00:03:21.791 --> 00:03:24.958
but the haziness of the mind makes it feel heavy

59
00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:27.041
and burdensome.

60
00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:30.458
At a tourist spot, two people

61
00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:32.291
look at you and laugh.

62
00:03:32.291 --> 00:03:34.250
You tense up,

63
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:38.000
thinking they are mocking you.

64
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.500
You build a wrong impression

65
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.500
about them and decide in your mind
to confront them.

66
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.125
But when you hear a noise

67
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.875
and turn around, you see –

68
00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:54.500
two monkeys doing amusing acrobatics nearby.

69
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.041
Those people were laughing at the monkeys.

70
00:03:59.041 --> 00:04:02.666
You had taken on the burden of
negative thinking for nothing.

71
00:04:02.666 --> 00:04:05.708
Tamo Guna confuses you.

72
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:09.750
And if you do not recognise it,
that very confusion

73
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.125
becomes your reality.

74
00:04:13.125 --> 00:04:15.125
But remember –

75
00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:18.500
you are not your thoughts.

76
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.250
You must become a gatekeeper.

77
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.583
Ask yourself –

78
00:04:24.583 --> 00:04:27.375
‘Is this thought helpful?

79
00:04:27.375 --> 00:04:29.375
Is it true?

80
00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:33.458
Is it bringing me closer to peace?’

81
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:35.750
If the answer is ‘no’ –

82
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.083
do not hold on to it.

83
00:04:38.083 --> 00:04:42.291
Just as clouds pass through the sky,

84
00:04:42.291 --> 00:04:44.500
let it pass.

85
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.375
And when you let it go,

86
00:04:47.375 --> 00:04:52.250
you will find Me behind the noise –

87
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.750
clear, calm, and unwavering.

88
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:04.250
Have you ever wondered –

89
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.625
why do people living under the same roof

90
00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:12.375
sometimes begin to feel like strangers?

91
00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:15.083
It is not always due to big arguments

92
00:05:15.083 --> 00:05:17.750
or differences.

93
00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.666
Often the reason is very simple –

94
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:25.583
no one taking the first step.

95
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:29.083
This is apravritti –

96
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:33.291
a subtle effect of Tamo Guna.

97
00:05:33.291 --> 00:05:36.125
It does not come with noise.

98
00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:39.875
It shows itself when you know

99
00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:43.208
you should check on someone,

100
00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.708
say a kind word,

101
00:05:45.708 --> 00:05:49.416
or offer a little help –

102
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:53.125
but you put it off. And slowly

103
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:57.250
this inaction becomes a habit.

104
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.000
A child waits

105
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.166
for a parent to ask –

106
00:06:02.166 --> 00:06:07.375
‘How was your day at school?’

107
00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:09.250
A spouse wants

108
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.083
to be noticed.

109
00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:16.500
An elder wants their words to be heard.

110
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.791
But everyone remains silent –

111
00:06:18.791 --> 00:06:23.458
not from indifference, but because Tamo Guna

112
00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:26.708
makes the mind and heart sluggish.

113
00:06:26.708 --> 00:06:29.833
Understand this –

114
00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.000
love in a family

115
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:35.083
does not fade because it ends.

116
00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:36.791
It weakens

117
00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:41.791
because it stops being expressed.

118
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:42.750
So whether

119
00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.583
it is simply sitting quietly beside someone,

120
00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:50.166
or offering a warm smile –

121
00:06:50.166 --> 00:06:53.125
take that first step.

122
00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:55.041
This small act

123
00:06:55.041 --> 00:06:57.541
brings light into the home

124
00:06:57.541 --> 00:07:00.958
where the lamp of love exists –

125
00:07:00.958 --> 00:07:04.916
but waits to be lit by the flame of expression.

126
00:07:04.916 --> 00:07:08.833
Do not delay in speaking words of affection.

127
00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:13.291
This small step is auspicious for both you

128
00:07:13.291 --> 00:07:16.208
and the one who receives it.

129
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:17.666
Reflect on this.

130
00:07:22.583 --> 00:07:25.916
Have you ever seen a meeting

131
00:07:25.916 --> 00:07:29.250
where everything appears calm –

132
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:32.583
no objection, no disagreement,

133
00:07:32.583 --> 00:07:36.041
and no real contribution?

134
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:40.708
On the surface it may seem like peace.

135
00:07:40.708 --> 00:07:42.750
But think –

136
00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:47.291
is this truly peace… or apravritti?

137
00:07:47.291 --> 00:07:51.625
When Tamo Guna is dominant, it brings

138
00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:53.375
apravritti –

139
00:07:53.375 --> 00:07:59.500
indifference to work, and
pramada – carelessness.

140
00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.791
At the workplace,

141
00:08:00.791 --> 00:08:04.083
this does not show up as open resistance.

142
00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.958
It comes in very subtle forms.

143
00:08:06.958 --> 00:08:10.458
Work not completed on time.

144
00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:14.000
An email left unanswered.

145
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.625
A project slipping behind –

146
00:08:16.625 --> 00:08:20.000
not because people did not know,

147
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.000
but because no one took the initiative.

148
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.458
Sometimes you too may experience it –

149
00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:30.708
a long task list in front of you,

150
00:08:30.708 --> 00:08:35.416
but the mind simply does not want to begin.

151
00:08:35.416 --> 00:08:37.750
This is not rest.

152
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.666
This is stagnation.

153
00:08:39.666 --> 00:08:45.000
If a stitch in a garment comes loose,

154
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.166
it is best to sew it immediately.

155
00:08:48.166 --> 00:08:51.833
Otherwise, when the cloth catches

156
00:08:51.833 --> 00:08:54.791
on a table corner,

157
00:08:54.791 --> 00:08:57.791
the entire seam comes undone

158
00:08:57.791 --> 00:09:01.625
and the garment must go to the tailor.

159
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:04.958
If this becomes the team’s permanent tone,

160
00:09:04.958 --> 00:09:10.375
its culture slowly becomes hollow.

161
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:13.333
No one intended harm –

162
00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:17.041
but no one stayed alert either.

163
00:09:17.041 --> 00:09:19.583
So remember –

164
00:09:19.583 --> 00:09:22.416
progress does not always make noise.

165
00:09:22.416 --> 00:09:25.000
But it should not remain silent

166
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.458
due to neglect either.

167
00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:31.875
Your alertness is your contribution.

168
00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:34.250
Be present at the workplace –

169
00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.333
with energy and purpose.

170
00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:40.166
This is respect for your work…

171
00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:44.500
and respect for your soul.
